---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const origin = Astro.site.href.replace(/\/$/, "");
const title = "Data Visualisation | Studio Narrm, Melbourne";
const description = "Interactive data visualisation examples from Studio Narrm: a classic analytics dashboard plus ten creative charts, from radial timelines and beeswarms to sankeys, hex maps and chord diagrams.";
const jsonld = [{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "Data visualisation",
  "url": `${origin}/data-viz/`,
  "description": "Interactive data visualisation examples from Studio Narrm: a classic analytics dashboard plus ten creative charts, from radial timelines and beeswarms to sankeys, hex maps and chord diagrams.",
  "author": {
    "@id": `${origin}/#person`
  },
  "about": [
    "Data visualisation",
    "Dashboards",
    "D3.js",
    "Analytics"
  ],
  "breadcrumb": {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": `${origin}/`
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Data visualisation",
        "item": `${origin}/data-viz/`
      }
    ]
  }
}];
import "../../styles/data-viz.css";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} jsonld={jsonld} current="data-viz" includeBase={true}>
<main class="dv">
  <div class="dv-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Data visualisation</span>
      <h1>From a reliable dashboard to data people remember.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Most teams need two things from their data. They need a dashboard they can trust every morning, and sometimes a way to tell a story that sticks. We build both. Hover, click and filter anything below.</p>
      <span class="note">Every chart on this page uses fictional sample data</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="dash-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">01 · The everyday dashboard</span>
          <h2 id="dash-h">Trends, comparisons and shares, at a glance</h2>
        </div>
        <p>This is the dashboard most software ships with: headline numbers, a trend over time, a breakdown by category and a share of the whole. We can set one up like this for any analytics you want to track, fed automatically from your systems.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="dash">
        <div class="dash-bar">
          <b>Sample Co. · Sales overview</b>
          <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Date range">
            <button type="button" data-days="30" aria-pressed="false">30 days</button>
            <button type="button" data-days="90" aria-pressed="true">90 days</button>
            <button type="button" data-days="365" aria-pressed="false">12 months</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpis" id="kpis"></div>
        <div class="dash-grid">
          <div class="panel"><h4>Revenue trend <span>· daily, AUD</span></h4><div id="d-line"></div></div>
          <div class="panel"><h4>Revenue by segment</h4><div id="d-donut"></div><div class="legend" id="d-donut-legend"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dash-grid">
          <div class="panel"><h4>Revenue by channel</h4><div id="d-bar"></div></div>
          <div class="panel"><h4>Orders by weekday</h4><div id="d-week"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="explain">
        <div><b>Connected to your data</b>Pulled from your CRM, spreadsheets, forms or database on a schedule, so nobody updates it by hand.</div>
        <div><b>Built in the tool you use</b>Looker Studio, Power BI or a custom web app, depending on who needs it and where.</div>
        <div><b>Numbers people agree on</b>Every metric is defined once, so the dashboard ends arguments instead of starting them.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="gal-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">02 · Beyond the dashboard</span>
          <h2 id="gal-h">Ten creative ways to show data</h2>
        </div>
        <p>When the goal is to explain, persuade or delight, a different shape often tells the story better. Each of these is interactive and is inspired by the style of a piece we admire.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery" id="gallery"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="cta-end">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Have data that deserves better?</h2>
      <p>Tell us what you're tracking and who needs to see it. We'll suggest the simplest view that works, from a dashboard to something more creative.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/#contact">Talk about your data</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
<div id="tip" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>

<script is:inline slot="scripts" src="/assets/vendor/d3.min.js"></script>
<script is:inline slot="scripts" src="/assets/vendor/d3-sankey.min.js"></script>
<script is:inline slot="scripts" src="/assets/data-viz.js"></script>
</Base>
